			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4837936">
									

<p>Some day &quot;I can fix this&quot; will be uttered by a character undergoing a crisis, and they will be able to fix whatever this is. Today is not that day.</p>
<p>Very well done, overall. Compelling action, good call-backs, oodles of character development, and some interesting turns that, while not out of left field, still feel surprising. With halfway left for the rest of this cycle, I am very, very interested to see where it goes, in a way that I haven't been for a series in some time.</p>
<p>My one complaint is that the description of various characters is so distinctive that it's very obvious when you are cribbing from previous works, sometimes word for word (Medea has &quot;shoulder-length brunette hair and faint blue eyes&quot;; Jason has &quot;mop of curly blond hair; Jeffery is &quot;a middle-aged man with dark skin&quot;; Anderson has &quot;triangular grating that rapidly hissed with the passage of air&quot; and &quot;two small camera lenses that glowed with a faint green light&quot;). They aren't bad descriptions, but it was a shame to be jerked out of the narrative several times by the realization that &quot;hey, wait, didn't Conwell already say this?&quot;</p>
<p>Still, an easy +1</p>

